        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>triangulate hole boundary loops of <computeroutput>mesh</computeroutput> in the mesh's own 3d space, orienting faces around <computeroutput>normal</computeroutput> combinatorics run on the dominant-axis projection of <computeroutput>normal</computeroutput>; output vertices keep the exact mesh coordinates (no projection round-trip), and loops sharing a mesh vertex are merged by identity. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>loops</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>one closed EdgeLoop per contour (as produced by trackRightBoundaryLoop on each hole edge) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>outPatchMap</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>optional output: for each patch boundary edge (by undirected id) the mesh edge it copies, directed along it; edges past its size are the triangulation's own </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>std::nullopt if the loops self-intersect, otherwise the patch mesh Generated from function <computeroutput><ref refid="classMR_1_1PlanarTriangulation_1aa43721ee35ac47b736aab3533b4bf7a0" kindref="member">MR.PlanarTriangulation.triangulateDisjointContours</ref></computeroutput>. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
